Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "path": identify file type via its extension (.py, .r) in GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES  
• "id": join key between SAMPLE_FILES and SAMPLE_CONTENTS in both tables  
• "content": actual source code to search for import / library statements in GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS  
• "repo_name": optional filter / grouping by repository in both tables  
• "sample_path": duplicate of file‑path field in SAMPLE_CONTENTS (useful when joining)  
• "sample_repo_name": duplicate of repo name in SAMPLE_CONTENTS  
Typical conditions  
• WHERE "path" ILIKE '%.py' OR "path" ILIKE '%.r'                    -- language selection  
• WHERE "content" ILIKE '%import %' OR "content" ILIKE '%library(%'   -- rough code filter  
• JOIN  GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES f  
         ON f."id" = c."id"                                           -- link file meta & content  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL statements (each returns ≤ 20 rows) that build understanding from simple inspection to extracting candidate module names.  
All identifiers are enclosed in double quotes.

